{
  "title": "Masked replication separates f35v fruit and foliage parallels and leaves some roots unscorable",
  "statement": "Two independent readers agreed on 145 of 156 outline calls including 35 shared unknowns, and on 110 of 111 jointly definite calls. Each identified all 12 features on the f35v image. They jointly scored all three fruit features on four of 12 comparator cards, two Sloane grape views, BnF Brionia, and Egerton black ivy. Dropping F2 added the BnF black ivy. The prior single-reader seven became four because F2 was uncertain on the BnF ivy and the fruit outlines were unresolved on both elder illustrations. Egerton Galla was the only comparator with all three lower-leaf features agreed. The BnF Galla's lower-leaf attachment was uncertain to one reader. No comparator showed the C3 crossing or either of the f35v root shapes by both readers. The highest definite comparator score was 6/12 for Egerton Galla. Treating every uncertain call as possibly matching raises the maximum to 11/12, driven by an isolated Glandes twig with 11 unresolved features, so the prior seven-point upper bound did not replicate. Dropping C3 preserves the fruit and leaf results. The three herbal manuscripts are related witnesses. This panel establishes regional outline similarities with limited botanical specificity.",
  "program": "L4",
  "check": "Prepare caption-masked full-height plant images from a separately catalogued herbal tradition and repeat the published 12-feature rubric with two independent readers, retaining unknowns. Include complete and edge-truncated roots and quantify how much censoring changes specificity. Report each fruit, leaf, crown and root score alongside the two-reader agreement and the separate results after excluding F2 and C3. Use no Voynich text readings.",
  "on_path": true,
  "hard": true,
