  "rubric": "Use only visible outlines. Color may locate a contour but adds no point. For each criterion record 1 when visible, 0 when clearly absent or discordant on a complete view, and ? when genuinely ambiguous or cropped. Record all 12 criteria across the whole card. Do not name plants or guess provenance.\n\nFruit (F)\nF1. At least two discrete clusters of three or more rounded enclosed units, counting each unit once; scattered solitary fruits do not count.\nF2. At least one such cluster terminates a distinct stalk, with recognizable grouping and no enclosing common fruit body or backing leaf.\nF3. No acorn-like cup, enclosing husk, or lobed capsule around the rounded units; mark unknown if outlines are unreadable, zero if no rounded units.\n\nLeaf (L)\nL1. At least two individually outlined side leaves attach at distinct levels below the top foliage.\nL2. Those side leaves are simple and visibly lobed, with at least two broad rounded lobes per side.\nL3. The strongest lobing repeats along the long axis on both sides of the leaf; do not count a three- to five-point palmate leaf, a smooth small leaf, or individual leaflets along a rachis.\n\nCrown/stems (C)\nC1. A compact upper foliage outline distinguishable from lower lateral leaves or fruit.\nC2. Multiple upward stalks fan toward that upper outline from a relatively narrow common point or band.\nC3. Two lower lateral stems visibly cross in front of or around a distinct upright axis; a single fork without crossing does not count.\n\nRoots (R)\nR1. Clearly drawn roots and aerial stems meet at a common basal junction.\nR2. Major lateral roots or primary branches bear at least three recognizable hooked or curved tips in aggregate.\nR3. Strongly asymmetric lateral spread, roughly 2:1 or greater from the stem center measured against opposite side, with the longest root roughly horizontal for much of its run.",
