  "native_scan_audit": {
    "02": "Native crops at XYWH [1220,180,1600,2140] and [500,2700,2300,1060] show separately attached lower lobed leaves, a crossing near the upright axis, branching at the root junction, and at least three visible recurved ends. The longest lateral root extends left at about three times the right reach from the junction. Fine contours near the sheet edge remain difficult.",
    "04": "The complete BnF ivy image runs to the lower sheet edge without revealing a root junction. The visible long basal roots belong to the left-hand plant.",
    "05": "In BnF Galla, the lower lateral foliage of the right-hand tree partly overlaps the crown. The trunk continues to the lower sheet edge without a legible root spread. The conspicuous roots on the left belong to another specimen.",
    "06": "On the complete BnF Brionia plate the long downward fork reaches the sheet edge. A junction is visible. The missing tips cannot be inferred from that outline, and the fork is chiefly vertical.",
    "07": "The BnF Ebulus lateral root arms extend to the sheet edges, leaving an unknown full extent and terminal shape despite the visible junction.",
    "09": "The Glandes is a short isolated marginal sprig with a cup. The wide root spread on the same sheet belongs to a separate plant, so the 11 unresolved calls cannot be lifted by including its roots.",
    "10": "Egerton Galla shows offset rounded-lobed lower blades below the upper foliage and a visible basal junction. The roots fan downward and lack the f35v horizontal imbalance. Some narrow terminals are faint.",
    "11": "The Egerton Ebulus does have a visible spread below its stalk. Its faint continuations into the parchment make terminal curvature and maximal reach uncertain.",
    "12": "Egerton Brionia has a large downward fork with both ends at the lower sheet edge. Native coverage leaves the contour terminals unresolved.",
    "13": "The exposed basal line of Egerton ivy tapers to a point above its caption. A faint nearby mark does not establish a continuous root junction or a measurable root spread."
  },
